    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Tausug Muslim sultanate ruling the islands between Mindanao and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#borneo">Borneo</a> from Jolo, founded by tradition by Sharif ul-Hashim.</li><li>It resisted Spanish conquest for three centuries and grew rich exporting sea produce to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a> in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries.</li><li>Its 1878 grant of North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#borneo">Borneo</a> to a British syndicate is the origin of the Philippine claim to Sabah.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#paduka-batara">Paduka Batara</a>, a Sulu ruler who died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a> in 1417, is buried at Dezhou in Shandong; members of his family stayed to tend the tomb and their descendants still live there.</p></aside>
    </section>

